# The demands filed as a range. One row per layer whose demand spans a width, so there is
# something a narrowing statement could actually reduce.
#
# The base for a receiver's one fact
#   This is the base for the one number a receiver is entitled to state as a fact. Judging whether
#   a narrowing sentence would narrow the range is prose, and belongs to a person. Counting how many
#   ranges decline to say anything at all is arithmetic, and it turns "a claim without one is
#   weaker" from an opinion into a figure.
#
# The other side of the single-value rule
#   It lives here: a range that files `narrowsWhen` as `notApplicable` is claiming it has no range,
#   in a row that plainly has one.
-- pm:Claim on pm:Demand where low <> high.
SELECT d.*
FROM (
    :compose(layers/demand.sqlc)
) d
WHERE NOT d.is_a_point
